UPDATE tools SET faq = $x$[{"a": "Bubble is a no-code application builder — it's for building web apps with databases, logic, and user interactions. Webflow is a no-code website builder focused on design and CMS. Bubble builds apps; Webflow builds websites.", "q": "What is the difference between Bubble and Webflow?"}, {"a": "Webflow has a CMS (Content Management System) for structured content like blog posts and product listings. It's not a full application database — for user data, transactions, or complex logic, you'd need Bubble or a custom backend.", "q": "Does Webflow have a database?"}, {"a": "Webflow's Starter site plan and Starter Workspace are both free, and Bubble also has a free plan. Beyond that, the two charge differently: Webflow bills separately for a site plan (Basic starts at $15/mo billed yearly, $25/mo billed monthly) and a separate paid Workspace plan that bundles AI credits, plus optional seats and add-ons, while Bubble charges per app workload. A direct cost comparison depends on which tiers and add-ons you combine.", "q": "Which is cheaper — Bubble or Webflow?"}]$x$::jsonb
