 WHERE slug = 'relume' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Relume is an AI-powered website planning and building tool aimed at agencies, freelancers, and designers. Describe a site's purpose and audience, and Relume generates a brief, a full sitemap, and detailed wireframes for each page, which can be customized before export or publishing. The product now spans two offerings: 'Build with Relume,' an AI website builder, and 'Site Builder,' a component-library-driven wireframing tool.

The company recently repositioned itself: it moved its primary domain from relume.io to relume.ai, and launched a 'Publish' path (in beta since August 2026) that takes a project from brief to a live hosted site, with Relume handling the custom domain and SSL. This sits alongside the original 'Export' path, which now supports React (Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui) in addition to Webflow and Figma. In October 2026 Relume also introduced a Publish MCP that lets users build, publish, and update a full website in Relume from inside AI chat assistants such as Claude or ChatGPT, with handoff to Webflow, alongside a 'Component Day' update adding animated hero headers and new sections.

Key capabilities include AI-generated briefs, sitemaps, and wireframes, a style guide generator, unlimited collaboration, and a component library of 1,000+ pre-built sections (hero, features, pricing, FAQ, etc.) available across Webflow, Figma, and React. The free tier of Build with Relume includes free hosting on a relume.live subdomain with up to 1,500 page views and 20 form submissions per month, plus a Relume badge; the free tier of Site Builder includes 30 Webflow components, 30 React components, and 1,000+ Figma components.

Pricing is split across the two products. Build with Relume has a free plan (no card required, limited shared AI usage, unlimited websites, relume.live hosting) and a Pro plan starting from $14/month with a premium AI model and priority access; hosting on a custom domain through the Launch feature is priced separately, starting at $12/project/month. Site Builder has a free plan and paid tiers: Starter from $18/month, Pro from $40/month (1,000+ components across all platforms, up to 300 component storage), Team from $36/month per user with a 3-user minimum, and a custom-priced Enterprise tier. All published prices use a 'From $X/month' structure, so the final cost depends on configuration; no annual-billing discount is currently published.

Limitations: the Publish path is still in beta, and using it means the live site runs on Relume's own hosting rather than an existing platform. It is also unclear which plans include the new Publish MCP. The Export path still requires a separate Webflow or Figma account for that workflow, and exact final pricing for any tier depends on usage and configuration rather than a single flat number.

Relume suits agencies, freelancers, and designers who want to accelerate the planning and wireframing phase of a web project, whether they intend to hand off to Webflow, Figma, or React, or publish directly through Relume's own beta hosting.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'relume' AND lang = 'en';

