UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Claude Design is a built-in Claude feature, available on every Claude plan including Free, that generates UI mockups, presentations, dashboards-style visuals and prototypes directly inside a Claude conversation, Claude Code, or the Artifacts tab.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude-design' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Claude Design is a design capability built into Claude rather than a separate paid product. It works inside any Claude conversation, in Claude Code, and from the Artifacts tab, turning a team's codebase and design files, or a plain chat request, into visual design output.

It moved into regular Claude chat on September 16, 2026 and came out of beta on October 8, 2026, when Anthropic made it available on every plan, including Free. The previous standalone site at claude.ai/design is being retired and closes on December 14, 2026, after which all design work happens inside normal Claude chats. For Enterprise accounts it has been on by default since October 15, 2026, except for HIPAA-enabled organizations; admins can still control the setting. Anthropic does not publicly name the model powering the feature.

Claude Design can read an existing codebase and design files to build a reusable design system, and exports finished work as a .zip, PDF, PPTX, Google Slides file, or standalone HTML. It can also send output directly to connected tools including Adobe Experience Manager, Adobe for Creativity, Adobe Journey Optimizer, Base44, Canva, Gamma, HubSpot, Hyperframes, Lovable, Miro, Netlify, Replit, v0, Vercel and Wix, and can hand off to Claude Code using the /design-sync or /design commands.

There is no separate price for Claude Design; it is bundled into every Claude plan, including the Free plan at $0. Paid plans are Pro at $20/month ($17/month billed annually), Max starting from $100/month, Team Standard at $25/seat/month ($20/seat/month billed annually), Team Premium at $125/seat/month ($100/seat/month billed annually), and Enterprise at $20/seat/month billed annually plus usage at API rates. Since moving into chat, all Claude Design activity counts toward the plan's shared usage limits, and the earlier separate weekly Claude Design allowance has been removed; larger design requests use up more of that shared limit.

The underlying model isn't disclosed, the standalone site is being phased out in favor of in-chat use, and exact Max-tier pricing above the $100/month starting point isn't published. It suits anyone already using Claude, from Free-plan users experimenting with AI-generated visuals to product teams and Enterprise organizations that want a consistent design system generated from their own code and files.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude-design' AND lang = 'en';

